# Locally-rebuilt DSpark drafters (2.5 GB of weights, hardlinked to one copy).
# These are Doopeworld/Qwen3.8-27B-DSpark-vLLM with a single edited field —
# config.json's `block_size` — so vLLM will accept a num_speculative_tokens
# below the published 7. Regenerate with the recipe in README.md rather than
# committing weights.
drafters/

# GuideLLM's raw per-request dumps: ~11-16 MB each, 140 MB total, and they hold
# one record per request rather than anything you would read. The numbers that
# matter are already in benchmarks/RESULTS.log, benchmarks/PROD.log and each
# run's console.txt, all of which ARE committed. Regenerate with gllm.sh.
benchmarks/guidellm/**/benchmarks.json
benchmarks/guidellm/benchmarks.json

# The repo root ignores *.log, but these two ARE the results — RESULTS.log is
# one line per single-stream run and PROD.log one line per concurrency run, and
# README.md points at both as the record of what was actually measured
# (including the runs that OOMed, hung or died).
!benchmarks/RESULTS.log
!benchmarks/PROD.log
# Same reasoning: ACCURACY.log is the GSM8K record the SGLang tuning section
# cites, including the n=300 rows that turned out to be wrong, and SCALING.log
# is the per-run record the scaling-grid section cites.
!benchmarks/ACCURACY.log
!benchmarks/SCALING.log
